{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/217970-movies-to-watch-while-drunk","id":217970,"title":"Movies to watch while Drunk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-04T01:42:09-07:00","id":217970,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Movies to watch while Drunk","content":"This might already be a thread, if so I apologize. I know there's threads about movies, but which ones do you like to watch while playing Drinking games or just seem better once you're buzzed? You can even though out there movies that are your picks for after clubbing/pub crawl something-to-watch-till-you-pass-out movies.<br /> <br /> Friends and I seem to get blitzed every time we get someone new in our circle to watch Tropic Thunder for the first time.<br /> <br /> I have a fond memory related to a time when I had just gotten some bad news and felt horrible and rejected, only for my brother to come hang out with me and cheer me up pouring me Screwdrivers and showing me Wall-E for the first time. (I'd missed it in theaters) but it didn't stop there. We were both well and truly drunk when he put on Sweeny Todd Demon Barber of fleet street. I'll never forget singing &quot;A Little Priest&quot; with my bro at 3am willfully neglectful of noise ordinances and neighbors.<br /> <br /> Of course there's many others like Beerfest, Fight Club and Superbad that seems to be what everyone gets drunk to. Anyone care to post about any other movies and the stories that go with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><